  "body": "Access-request cards currently identify the feature and request number but omit who submitted the request. This change displays `Solicitante: <name>` on the user's request list and on review cards in every status, including approved requests.\n\nThe API resolves `requesterName` from the requester's Party display name within the existing requester/reviewer authorization scope. New reviewer notifications include that name. Missing or blank names show a localized fallback, and the UI also tolerates older API responses during rollout. Existing notification bodies are not rewritten; existing request cards obtain the name when loaded. No database migration is required.\n\nThe OpenAPI schema and both generated clients are synchronized. The mobile submodule advances by a single commit containing only the generated field; no mobile behavior changes.\n\nValidation: all 12 focused UI tests pass, covering five request statuses, missing/blank/legacy names, submission and accessibility. Production UI build (TypeScript, Vite and bundle budget), focused ESLint and the catalog-list audit pass. Both generated clients match the canonical OpenAPI schema. Chromium verified pending and approved cards at desktop (1440px) and mobile (390px) widths against the production build with synthetic session/API fixtures; this is not a live-authentication or deployed-backend test. All applicable hosted checks pass on `efb09219be25941af574eaac4ec5d2e7e3a421b2`, including backend build/tests and runtime checks, full UI/mobile quality, API contracts, repository/catalog checks, persona browser journeys and Cloudflare/Vercel previews. The backend job completed successfully in 41m09s. The guarded backend release plan also passes in dry-run mode; it has not been executed.\n\nDeployment requires the updated API and UI. Production has not been changed.\n",
